          "id": "92a679a13268a3bac646b5a98db60f7f54391561",
          "message": "bench(gsp): Graph Store Protocol same-box panel — sparq-server vs Fuseki GSP / Oxigraph GSP (+ CSS loose) (sq-hmd7l.21) [FABLE-5] (#1908)\n\nbench/gsp/: PUT/GET/DELETE round-trips over a deterministic 1KB-10MB\nresource-size sweep + the PSS LDP-CRUD stream projected onto GSP verbs,\nloopback-only (the driver hard-refuses non-loopback URLs, no bypass).\nHARD round-trip content gate BEFORE timing: returned triple SET must\nequal the PUT set exactly (ground bnode-free payloads, so set equality\nis isomorphism); CRUD final state must match a client-side reference\nmodel. The gate is itself regression-tested hermetically (--self-test:\nan honest fake store passes, a tampering store that drops a triple on\nread fails). CSS rides as a LOOSE LDP-architecture column — labelled on\nevery row, never averaged with the like-for-like Fuseki/Oxigraph\ncolumns.\n\nAcceptance: bash bench/gsp/run.sh --smoke exits 0 (sparq loopback,\nself-test + round-trip gates green). Registry: gsp-bench stub filled in\nbenchmarks.toml; fuseki/oxigraph comparable_suites gain gsp-bench;\nCATALOG.md care-note. First-read gap record (NON-canonical, no numbers\ntranscribed): research/gap-gsp-2026-07.md. Follow-ups beaded:\nsq-hmd7l.35 (canonical quiet-box gather run), sq-hmd7l.36 (PATCH-dialect\npanel).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
