          "message": "docs(policy): document odrl:conflict unset-default=prohibit divergence from the ODRL 2.2 IM default (sq-zjtu1) (#1912)\n\n* docs(policy): document the odrl:conflict unset-default=prohibit divergence from the ODRL 2.2 IM default of invalid (sq-zjtu1) [FABLE-5]\n\nAdopts and documents the Option-1 decision from issue #1375 (keep\ndeny-overrides as the unset default; disclose the spec divergence):\n\n- crates/sparq-policy/README.md: new \"ODRL conformance note\" — an unset\n  odrl:conflict operates under deny-overrides (odrl:prohibit), not the\n  ODRL 2.2 IM default of odrl:invalid; intentional because deny-overrides\n  is fail-closed (never authorises what a prohibition forbids). Stub stays\n  at the 30-line cap (License section compressed to one line).\n- site/papers/odrl-policy-bridge.typ: Limitation #1 was STALE — it still\n  said the bridge \"does not consult odrl:conflict\", that odrl:perm is\n  \"silently processed\" under prohibit, and that loud refusal is \"tracked\n  future work\". sq-ihqbl landed that refusal (perm / invalid-with-conflict\n  / unknown are refused before materialisation), so Limitation #1, §4.2,\n  the abstract, contribution C2, and the §3 comparison table are updated:\n  the remaining divergence is the UNSET default only. Revision note added\n  to the header comment; all 9 papers still compile.\n- skills/usage-control-policy/SKILL.md + compare.rs rustdoc: the honest\n  boundary no longer says \"tracked as a follow-up\" — the divergence is now\n  a decided, documented boundary (issue #1375).\n\nDocs only — no behavioural change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(skill): fix mis-attributed conflict default in usage-control-policy SKILL (sq-zjtu1) [FABLE-5]\n\nThe evaluation-semantics list credited prohibition-overrides to an \"ODRL\nFormal Semantics conflict default\"; the CG report's conflict machinery is\nexplicitly pending (per the paper's verified normative reading), so no\ndefault can be attributed to it. Reworded to name deny-overrides as the\none implemented strategy and point at the crate README's conformance note.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
